otnet_build_calls": 0, "edit_calls": 1, "ended_on_rejection": false, "error": null, "exec_mode": "local", "failure_class": "solved", "failure_reason": null, "faults_served": 0, "final_answer_complete": true, "final_answer_present": true, "final_answer_source": "json", "final_workspace": "/workspace/openbench-ab/results/omp-cap30-b2/cap30-44/omp-44/cells/with/trig-omp-multistep/4/workspace", "fresh_subagents": 0, "harness": "omp", "harness_version": "omp/18.3.0 (/workspace/pi-check/cache5/bin/omp/d3e08e91b65a46fc6d88bbb8ba641b6047172ce5/omp)", "harness_version_source": "host", "host": "grok-bot-vm-412615941", "image_digest": null, "last_activity_age_s": null, "list_has_generated": null, "main_agent_searched": false, "model": "claude-opus-5-5", "model_context_window": 1000000, "model_max_tokens": 128000, "output_tail": "Bug is in `to_cents`: `int(amount * 100)` truncates float error (`19.99*100 == 1998.9999\u2026` \u2192 1998). Round instead, via Decimal to avoid binary float artifacts.\npytest isn't installed, so I'll call the test functions directly.\nI fixed the bug in `ledger/currency.py`. `to_cents` computed `int(amount * 100)`, which chops off the decimals instead of rounding. Floats can't store prices like 19.99 exactly (`19.99 * 100` is `1998.9999\u2026`), so you got 1998 instead of 1999. The same thing happened with 0.29 and 4.35, which broke all four tests.\n\nNow `to_cents` converts the amount to a `Decimal` using its string form, multiplies by 100, and rounds half up to a whole number of cents.\n\npytest isn't installed here, so I called each test function in `tests/test_totals.py` and `tests/test_report.py` directly from Python, and all 5 passed. I haven't run the files under pytest itself.", "paced_wait_s": 0.0, "permission_rejections": 0, "read_calls": 8, "replies_ok": 6, "replies_throttled": 0, "requests_cache_read": 61798, "requests_cache_write": 15939, "requests_cost_usd": 0.1278106, "requests_count": 6, "requests_input_uncached": 14, "requests_outpu